==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|frm|manœuvre||manipulation, manoeuvre}} and {{m|frm|manouvrer||to manoeuvre}}, from {{der|en|fro|manovre||handwork, manual labour}}, from {{der|en|la-med|manopera}}, {{m|la|manuopera||work done by hand, handwork}}, from {{m|la|manu||by hand}} + {{m|la|operari||to work}}. First recorded in the Capitularies of Charlemagne (800 AD) to mean "chore, manual task", probably as a calque of the {{der|en|frk|*handwerc||hand-work}}. Compare {{cog|ang|handweorc}}, {{cog|ang|handġeweorc}}, {{cog|de|Handwerk}}.

===Pronunciation===
